//RS /// D-SYNC1: SyncText is a sequence CRDT, not a copy per replica.  Every
//RS /// character is one atom carrying a unique `(replica, counter)` identity and
//RS /// the identity of the atom it follows.  Reading order is recomputed from
//RS /// those identities, so a merge is the union of two atom sets with deletions
//RS /// winning: commutative, associative, and idempotent.  Two replicas that edit
//RS /// while apart converge on one document, and neither loses characters.
