//RS /// Invalid CRDT carriers are an absorbing denial state.  Their codec marker
//RS /// must round-trip that state instead of turning it into an ordinary shape
//RS /// error, otherwise a denied value could become an apparent decode failure at
//RS /// a tier boundary and lose the carrier's algebraic identity.
